{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_14","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"sed -n '150,240p' /home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1967842053/9/prompt.md\"","aggregated_output":"\nInput structure:\n- The background is the dominant color.\n- Each foreground object is a straight horizontal or vertical 4-connected rod.\n- Each rod contains many pixels of one line color, one endpoint marker, and one\n  interior control marker.\n\nRule:\n- For every rod, keep the segment from the endpoint marker through the control\n  marker unchanged.\n- Move the line-color tail on the far side of the control marker to a\n  perpendicular ray starting next to that marker.\n- Choose the perpendicular direction with more space to the grid edge.\n\nKey insight:\n- The endpoint marker identifies the fixed side of the rod, while the control\n  marker is the hinge; the tail folds into the larger open half-plane.\n</description>\n</reference_puzzle>\n\n<reference_puzzle index=\"9\" source=\"eval\" puzzle_id=\"dbff022c\" lines=\"275-288\">\n<description>\nFill hollow sprites' interiors using a color-palette legend on the grid edge.\n\nInput structure:\n- bg = most common color. Several hollow sprites with distinct border colors.\n- A small 2×N or N×2 palette block sits on one grid edge; one row/column lists border colors, the other lists corresponding fill colors.\n\nRule:\n- Locate the palette legend on a grid edge and read it as a border→fill color mapping.\n- Find enclosed bg regions (holes) inside sprites that don't touch the grid boundary.\n- For each hole, identify the most common adjacent border color, look it up in the palette, and fill the hole with the mapped fill color.\n\nKey insight: The palette's edge position and orientation determine reading direction; border colors in the palette uniquely key into fill colors.\n</description>\n</reference_puzzle>\n\n<reference_puzzle index=\"10\" source=\"train\" puzzle_id=\"3d6c6e23\" lines=\"10-27\">\n<description>\nMove each vertical stream of pixels into a bottom-aligned centered pile.\n\nInput structure\n- A mostly background grid contains one or more vertical source columns of\n  foreground pixels.\n- Each source column has n^2 foreground pixels, and the top-to-bottom color\n  sequence splits into monochrome groups of lengths 1, 3, 5, ...\n\nRule\n- Clear the canvas to background.\n- For each source column, read the foreground colors from top to bottom and\n  rebuild them at the bottom below the same column as odd-width centered\n  rows of lengths 1, 3, 5, ...\n\nKey insight\n- The scattered vertical pixels are falling grains; a square number of\n  grains decomposes into the odd row widths of a centered pyramid.\n</description>\n</reference_puzzle>\n\n<reference_puzzle index=\"11\" source=\"eval\" puzzle_id=\"6ffbe589\" lines=\"83-98\">\n<description>\nCrop a board cluster and rotate its color layers based on outside cue sprites.\n\nInput structure:\n- bg = most common color.\n- A main multi-color board cluster (largest foreground region).\n- Small monochrome cue sprites outside the board for the colors that rotate.\n\nRule:\n- Tight-crop around the board cluster.\n- For each color layer inside the crop, find its same-color cue outside.\n- Rotate that layer clockwise by (cue pixel count mod 4) × 90°.\n- No outside cue → no rotation.\n\nKey insight: Cue sprite size mod 4 encodes rotation amount for its matching color layer.\n</description>\n</reference_puzzle>\n\n<reference_puzzle index=\"12\" source=\"train\" puzzle_id=\"7ec998c9\" lines=\"14-28\">\n<description>\nDraw a blue folded corner-to-corner route through the lone marker's column.\n\nInput structure:\n- A rectangular grid filled with one background color.\n- Exactly one non-background marker pixel; blue is absent from the input.\n\nRule:\n- Preserve the marker and repaint background pixels in its column blue from top to bottom.\n- If the marker is in the unique center column, connect that column to the top-right and bottom-left corners.\n- Otherwise, connect the column to the top-left and bottom-right corners.\n\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
